{"answer": "The **PMA0 register** controls **data access cacheability**. Specifically, **CPUx Data Access CacheabilityRegister (PMA0)** defines whether a given physical address segment is seen as cacheable for **data accesses**: *“If bit n in the register is set then segment-n will be seen as cacheable for data accesses.”* [S1]", "base_url": "https://api.openai.com/v1", "candidate_k": 8, "chunks": "data/chunks_mixed_multi_slice.jsonl", "collection": "technical_docs", "dry_run": false, "embedding_model": "BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5", "mode": "hybrid", "model": "gpt-5.4-nano", "question": "Which PMA0 register controls data access cacheability?", "rrf_k": 60, "sources": [{"bm25_rank": 1, "bm25_score": 15.775745775473322, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 190, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 1, "id": "S1", "page_end": 257, "page_start": 257, "score": -0.03278688524590164, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 1}, {"bm25_rank": 2, "bm25_score": 15.327028869684177, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 191, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 2, "id": "S2", "page_end": 258, "page_start": 258, "score": -0.03225806451612903, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 2}, {"bm25_rank": 3, "bm25_score": 10.841043920363257, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 192, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 3, "id": "S3", "page_end": 259, "page_start": 259, "score": -0.031746031746031744, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 3}, {"bm25_rank": null, "bm25_score": null, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 200, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 4, "id": "S4", "page_end": 312, "page_start": 312, "score": -0.015625, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 4}, {"bm25_rank": 4, "bm25_score": 7.936750544295702, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 236, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 5, "id": "S5", "page_end": 1395, "page_start": 1395, "score": -0.015625, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": null}], "timestamp": "2026-05-26T18:13:53.201882+00:00", "token_param": "max_completion_tokens", "top_k": 5}
{"answer": "The **PMA1 (CPUx Code Access CacheabilityRegister)** controls **code access cacheability**. Specifically, **if bit n is set in PMA1, then segment-n is seen as cacheable for code accesses** [S1].", "base_url": "https://api.openai.com/v1", "candidate_k": 8, "chunks": "data/chunks_mixed_multi_slice.jsonl", "collection": "technical_docs", "dry_run": false, "embedding_model": "BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5", "mode": "hybrid", "model": "gpt-5.4-nano", "question": "Which PMA1 register controls code access cacheability?", "rrf_k": 60, "sources": [{"bm25_rank": 1, "bm25_score": 18.51834252345727, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 191, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 1, "id": "S1", "page_end": 258, "page_start": 258, "score": -0.03278688524590164, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 1}, {"bm25_rank": 3, "bm25_score": 9.699150317713816, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 190, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 2, "id": "S2", "page_end": 257, "page_start": 257, "score": -0.03200204813108039, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 2}, {"bm25_rank": 2, "bm25_score": 13.905914625870095, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 192, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 3, "id": "S3", "page_end": 259, "page_start": 259, "score": -0.031754032258064516, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 4}, {"bm25_rank": null, "bm25_score": null, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 200, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 4, "id": "S4", "page_end": 312, "page_start": 312, "score": -0.015873015873015872, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 3}, {"bm25_rank": 4, "bm25_score": 7.030774221665464, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 236, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 5, "id": "S5", "page_end": 1395, "page_start": 1395, "score": -0.015625, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": null}], "timestamp": "2026-05-26T18:13:54.465507+00:00", "token_param": "max_completion_tokens", "top_k": 5}
{"answer": "When changing the PMA registers (PMA0/PMA1/PMA2), you must maintain coherency by performing the following synchronization steps:\n\n- Invalidate both the instruction cache and the data cache after updating the PMA register values. [S1]  \n- Execute a **DSYNC** instruction **immediately prior** to the **MTCR** (write) of the PMA register. [S1]  \n- Execute an **ISYNC** instruction **immediately following** the **MTCR**. [S1]  \n\nThese steps are required “to maintain coherency of the processors view of memory.” [S1]  \n\n(Additionally, the same DSYNC/ISYNC requirement is stated for PMA1 changes as well.) [S2]", "base_url": "https://api.openai.com/v1", "candidate_k": 8, "chunks": "data/chunks_mixed_multi_slice.jsonl", "collection": "technical_docs", "dry_run": false, "embedding_model": "BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5", "mode": "hybrid", "model": "gpt-5.4-nano", "question": "What synchronization instructions are required when changing PMA registers to maintain coherency?", "rrf_k": 60, "sources": [{"bm25_rank": 2, "bm25_score": 20.491777775059198, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 190, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 1, "id": "S1", "page_end": 257, "page_start": 257, "score": -0.03252247488101534, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 1}, {"bm25_rank": 1, "bm25_score": 21.026344437035892, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 191, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 2, "id": "S2", "page_end": 258, "page_start": 258, "score": -0.032266458495966696, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 3}, {"bm25_rank": 3, "bm25_score": 15.667465631935478, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 192, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 3, "id": "S3", "page_end": 259, "page_start": 259, "score": -0.03200204813108039, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 2}, {"bm25_rank": null, "bm25_score": null, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 201, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 4, "id": "S4", "page_end": 313, "page_start": 313, "score": -0.015625, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 4}, {"bm25_rank": 4, "bm25_score": 11.926043498392877, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 200, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 5, "id": "S5", "page_end": 312, "page_start": 312, "score": -0.015625, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": null}], "timestamp": "2026-05-26T18:13:57.038151+00:00", "token_param": "max_completion_tokens", "top_k": 5}
{"answer": "The following physical address segments are constrained to **non-cacheable data/code accesses** (irrespective of PMA register settings):\n\n- **Data accesses (non-cacheable):**\n  - **Segments-F and segment-E** are constrained to be **Peripheral space and hence non-cacheable** [S4].\n  - **Segment-A** is constrained to be **non-cacheable memory** [S4].\n  - **Segment-D and Segment[7-CORE_ID]** are constrained to be **non-cacheable for data accesses** [S4].\n\n- **Code accesses (non-cacheable):**\n  - **Segments-C and Segment[7-CORE_ID]** are constrained to be **non-cacheable for code accesses** [S2].", "base_url": "https://api.openai.com/v1", "candidate_k": 8, "chunks": "data/chunks_mixed_multi_slice.jsonl", "collection": "technical_docs", "dry_run": false, "embedding_model": "BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5", "mode": "hybrid", "model": "gpt-5.4-nano", "question": "Which address segments are constrained to non-cacheable data or code accesses?", "rrf_k": 60, "sources": [{"bm25_rank": null, "bm25_score": null, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 5, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 1, "id": "S1", "page_end": 92, "page_start": 92, "score": -0.01639344262295082, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 1}, {"bm25_rank": 1, "bm25_score": 37.01758711051401, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 191, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 2, "id": "S2", "page_end": 258, "page_start": 258, "score": -0.01639344262295082, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": null}, {"bm25_rank": null, "bm25_score": null, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 2, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 3, "id": "S3", "page_end": 91, "page_start": 91, "score": -0.016129032258064516, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 2}, {"bm25_rank": 2, "bm25_score": 29.38488213629894, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 190, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 4, "id": "S4", "page_end": 257, "page_start": 257, "score": -0.016129032258064516, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": null}, {"bm25_rank": null, "bm25_score": null, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 11, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 5, "id": "S5", "page_end": 92, "page_start": 92, "score": -0.015873015873015872, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 3}], "timestamp": "2026-05-26T18:13:59.189126+00:00", "token_param": "max_completion_tokens", "top_k": 5}
{"answer": "The PMI program cache (PCACHE) provides a **two-way set associative instruction cache** (“instruction stream”) for **cacheable program fetches** with **single-cycle access on cache hit** and a refill sequence on cache miss [S2]. It can be **globally invalidated** to support **software cache coherency** [S2].\n\nSoftware can invalidate the cache by **writing a ‘1’ to `PCON1.PCINV`** (this invalidation is performed over **64 cycles** by hardware, marking each PCACHE entry invalid) [S1]. The software can also determine whether invalidation is in progress by **reading `PCON1.PCINV`** [S1].", "base_url": "https://api.openai.com/v1", "candidate_k": 8, "chunks": "data/chunks_mixed_multi_slice.jsonl", "collection": "technical_docs", "dry_run": false, "embedding_model": "BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5", "mode": "hybrid", "model": "gpt-5.4-nano", "question": "What does the PMI program cache provide and how can software invalidate it?", "rrf_k": 60, "sources": [{"bm25_rank": 2, "bm25_score": 22.460528699947012, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 200, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 1, "id": "S1", "page_end": 312, "page_start": 312, "score": -0.03252247488101534, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 1}, {"bm25_rank": 1, "bm25_score": 24.334709864429485, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 198, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 2, "id": "S2", "page_end": 310, "page_start": 310, "score": -0.03252247488101534, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 2}, {"bm25_rank": 3, "bm25_score": 17.350826639819857, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 202, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 3, "id": "S3", "page_end": 314, "page_start": 314, "score": -0.03149801587301587, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 4}, {"bm25_rank": 4, "bm25_score": 15.66172309385593, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 199, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 4, "id": "S4", "page_end": 311, "page_start": 311, "score": -0.030330882352941176, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 8}, {"bm25_rank": 6, "bm25_score": 12.01137250374861, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 201, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 5, "id": "S5", "page_end": 313, "page_start": 313, "score": -0.030303030303030304, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 6}], "timestamp": "2026-05-26T18:14:02.564267+00:00", "token_param": "max_completion_tokens", "top_k": 5}
{"answer": "No. The PMI (Program Memory Interface) does **not** have automatic cache coherency support; software must provide cache coherency. [S1]", "base_url": "https://api.openai.com/v1", "candidate_k": 8, "chunks": "data/chunks_mixed_multi_slice.jsonl", "collection": "technical_docs", "dry_run": false, "embedding_model": "BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5", "mode": "hybrid", "model": "gpt-5.4-nano", "question": "Does the PMI provide automatic cache coherency support?", "rrf_k": 60, "sources": [{"bm25_rank": 1, "bm25_score": 23.706079435015727, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 200, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 1, "id": "S1", "page_end": 312, "page_start": 312, "score": -0.03278688524590164, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 1}, {"bm25_rank": null, "bm25_score": null, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 99, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 2, "id": "S2", "page_end": 101, "page_start": 101, "score": -0.016129032258064516, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 2}, {"bm25_rank": 2, "bm25_score": 23.450803010689594, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 198, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 3, "id": "S3", "page_end": 310, "page_start": 310, "score": -0.016129032258064516, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": null}, {"bm25_rank": null, "bm25_score": null, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 83, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 4, "id": "S4", "page_end": 99, "page_start": 99, "score": -0.015873015873015872, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 3}, {"bm25_rank": 3, "bm25_score": 9.237334494085278, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 225, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 5, "id": "S5", "page_end": 1385, "page_start": 1385, "score": -0.015873015873015872, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": null}], "timestamp": "2026-05-26T18:14:03.592923+00:00", "token_param": "max_completion_tokens", "top_k": 5}
{"answer": "When **Program Cache Bypass** is enabled via **PCON0.PCBYP**, the **PCACHE is bypassed** (default after reset), and CPU instruction fetches behave as follows [S1]:\n\n- A fetch request by the CPU to a **cacheable address** causes a **forced cache miss** [S1].\n- The cache controller then performs a **standard refill sequence** and supplies instruction **half-words using instruction streaming**, but **does not update PCACHE contents** [S1].\n- Any **valid cache lines already in PCACHE remain valid and unchanged** while bypass is enabled [S1].\n- As a result, **instruction fetches to cacheable addresses with bypass enabled behave identically to fetches from non-cacheable addresses** [S1].", "base_url": "https://api.openai.com/v1", "candidate_k": 8, "chunks": "data/chunks_mixed_multi_slice.jsonl", "collection": "technical_docs", "dry_run": false, "embedding_model": "BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5", "mode": "hybrid", "model": "gpt-5.4-nano", "question": "What happens when program cache bypass is enabled with PCON0 PCBYP?", "rrf_k": 60, "sources": [{"bm25_rank": 1, "bm25_score": 27.71328033716824, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 200, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 1, "id": "S1", "page_end": 312, "page_start": 312, "score": -0.03278688524590164, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 1}, {"bm25_rank": 4, "bm25_score": 10.419507828378801, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 193, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 2, "id": "S2", "page_end": 307, "page_start": 307, "score": -0.031754032258064516, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 2}, {"bm25_rank": 3, "bm25_score": 11.244992115018238, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 202, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 3, "id": "S3", "page_end": 314, "page_start": 314, "score": -0.031746031746031744, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 3}, {"bm25_rank": 6, "bm25_score": 9.558717686413717, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 199, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 4, "id": "S4", "page_end": 311, "page_start": 311, "score": -0.030776515151515152, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 4}, {"bm25_rank": 5, "bm25_score": 10.138864231809643, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 196, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 5, "id": "S5", "page_end": 308, "page_start": 308, "score": -0.030536130536130537, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 6}], "timestamp": "2026-05-26T18:14:05.639273+00:00", "token_param": "max_completion_tokens", "top_k": 5}
{"answer": "A software-generated DMA request is done by writing **CHCSR.SCH = 1B** for the DMA channel. This initiates the request such that **TSR.CH is set to 1B**; at the start of the DMA transaction the DMA channel reload value **CHCFGR.TREL** is loaded into **ME CHSR.TCOUNT**, and DMA transfers then execute. After the transfers complete, **TSR.CH is reset** (in particular, in Single Mode this happens when **CHSR.TCOUNT** decrements to **0D**). To start another software-controlled transaction/transfer, write **CHCSR.SCH = 1B** again. [S1]\n\nFor the behavior “single transfer vs complete transaction” under software control, configure **CHCFGR.RROAT**:\n- **CHCFGR.RROAT = 0B**: **TSR.CH cleared at the start of each DMA transfer**; **one DMA request starts one single DMA transfer**. [S2]\n- **CHCFGR.RROAT = 1B**: **TSR.CH cleared at the end of each DMA transaction**; **one DMA request starts one complete DMA transaction**. [S2]\n\nAlso note: during software-only triggering, **DMA Hardware Request should be disabled** by setting **TSR.DCH = 1B** (so **TSR.HTRE = 0B**). [S2]", "base_url": "https://api.openai.com/v1", "candidate_k": 8, "chunks": "data/chunks_mixed_multi_slice.jsonl", "collection": "technical_docs", "dry_run": false, "embedding_model": "BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5", "mode": "hybrid", "model": "gpt-5.4-nano", "question": "How can software generate a DMA request using CHCSR SCH?", "rrf_k": 60, "sources": [{"bm25_rank": 3, "bm25_score": 17.444406962372874, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 246, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 1, "id": "S1", "page_end": 1442, "page_start": 1442, "score": -0.032266458495966696, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 1}, {"bm25_rank": 1, "bm25_score": 18.691877504882235, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 245, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 2, "id": "S2", "page_end": 1441, "page_start": 1441, "score": -0.032266458495966696, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 3}, {"bm25_rank": 4, "bm25_score": 15.081005362914732, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 248, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 3, "id": "S3", "page_end": 1444, "page_start": 1444, "score": -0.03125, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 4}, {"bm25_rank": 2, "bm25_score": 17.801325842736794, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 252, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 4, "id": "S4", "page_end": 1447, "page_start": 1447, "score": -0.031054405392392875, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 7}, {"bm25_rank": 6, "bm25_score": 14.365958752502785, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 259, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 5, "id": "S5", "page_end": 1453, "page_start": 1453, "score": -0.030536130536130537, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 5}], "timestamp": "2026-05-26T18:14:08.402430+00:00", "token_param": "max_completion_tokens", "top_k": 5}
{"answer": "After each **DMA move**, the **next source and destination addresses** are **calculated independently** of each other. The address generation uses:\n\n- An **address offset** that is a **multiple of the selected data width**.\n- An **offset direction** that can be **addition**, **subtraction**, or **none** (address unchanged). [S1]\n- **Address control bits** in the DMA channel **ADICR** determine whether addresses increment or decrement, and the **data width** (**CHCFGR.CHDW**) is taken into account. [S1]\n- The **Address Offset Calculation Tables** specify the per-move offset values:\n  - **Source address** update uses **SMF** and **INCS** parameters.\n  - **Destination address** update uses **DMF** and **INCD** parameters.\n  These offsets are **added or subtracted** from the current source/destination addresses after each DMA move. [S1]", "base_url": "https://api.openai.com/v1", "candidate_k": 8, "chunks": "data/chunks_mixed_multi_slice.jsonl", "collection": "technical_docs", "dry_run": false, "embedding_model": "BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5", "mode": "hybrid", "model": "gpt-5.4-nano", "question": "How are DMA source and destination addresses calculated during a data move?", "rrf_k": 60, "sources": [{"bm25_rank": 1, "bm25_score": 30.786086226877682, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 260, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 1, "id": "S1", "page_end": 1454, "page_start": 1454, "score": -0.03278688524590164, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 1}, {"bm25_rank": 2, "bm25_score": 27.917431780641014, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 241, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 2, "id": "S2", "page_end": 1437, "page_start": 1437, "score": -0.03225806451612903, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 2}, {"bm25_rank": 3, "bm25_score": 26.34546242307777, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 242, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 3, "id": "S3", "page_end": 1438, "page_start": 1438, "score": -0.03149801587301587, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 4}, {"bm25_rank": 5, "bm25_score": 20.20486922621301, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 263, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 4, "id": "S4", "page_end": 1483, "page_start": 1483, "score": -0.03125763125763126, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 3}, {"bm25_rank": 4, "bm25_score": 23.065881415601797, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 266, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 5, "id": "S5", "page_end": 1486, "page_start": 1486, "score": -0.031009615384615385, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 5}], "timestamp": "2026-05-26T18:14:10.861734+00:00", "token_param": "max_completion_tokens", "top_k": 5}
{"answer": "After a DMA channel has entered the **reset state**, software must ensure the reset operation completes and then (if needed) restart the channel.\n\n- **Monitor the reset completion** by checking the **DMA channel reset bit** (**TSR.RST**) and the **SADR, DADR, SHADR** registers. The reset is completed **as soon as** `TSR.RST = 0B` and the **SADR/DADR/SHADR** registers have been reset. [S1]  \n- **Do not initiate a DMA Software Request during the DMA Channel Reset** (i.e., do not set **CHCSR.SCH = 1B** while the reset is ongoing). [S1]  \n- If you want to **restart after the reset**, restart requires:\n  - Configure **TCS** (including **double buffering** address pointers to the base address). [S1]\n  - Then issue either a **DMA Software Request** (`CHCSR.SCH = 1B`) or enable a **DMA Hardware Request** (`TSR.ECH = 1B`). [S1]", "base_url": "https://api.openai.com/v1", "candidate_k": 8, "chunks": "data/chunks_mixed_multi_slice.jsonl", "collection": "technical_docs", "dry_run": false, "embedding_model": "BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5", "mode": "hybrid", "model": "gpt-5.4-nano", "question": "What should software do after a DMA channel has entered the reset state?", "rrf_k": 60, "sources": [{"bm25_rank": 1, "bm25_score": 24.735685205596596, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 252, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 1, "id": "S1", "page_end": 1447, "page_start": 1447, "score": -0.03278688524590164, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 1}, {"bm25_rank": 3, "bm25_score": 19.824462232564937, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 246, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 2, "id": "S2", "page_end": 1442, "page_start": 1442, "score": -0.03125763125763126, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": 5}, {"bm25_rank": 8, "bm25_score": 17.9595274402754, "boosted_score": null, "chunk_index": 245, "chunk_type": null, "hybrid_rank": 3, "id": "S3", "page_end": 1441, "page_start": 1441, "score": -0.03083491